  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS), which provides persistent block storage volumes for use with Amazon EC2 instances. Option A, Amazon S3, is object storage. Option C, Amazon EFS, is a scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based EC2 instances. Option D, Amazon DynamoDB, is a NoSQL database service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_2_79',
  'What is the primary advantage of Amazon Aurora''s architecture for high availability?',
  'mcq',
  '["It automatically scales compute capacity based on demand.","It provides a single endpoint for both read and write operations.","It separates compute and storage, replicating data across three Availability Zones.","It allows for manual snapshot creation for disaster recovery."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) highlights Amazon Aurora''s key architectural advantage for high availability. Aurora''s storage is decoupled from compute and automatically replicates data six ways across three Availability Zones, providing high durability and fast failover. Option A describes Aurora''s scaling capabilities, but not its primary HA mechanism. Option B is partially true for the cluster endpoint but doesn''t explain the underlying HA. Option D is a feature of many AWS storage services, not unique to Aurora''s primary HA benefit.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  8,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_2_80',
  'Which AWS service can automatically adjust the number of Amazon EC2 instances in response to changing application load?',
  'mcq',
