  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Direct Connect, which establishes a dedicated private network connection from your premises to AWS, bypassing the public internet for consistent low-latency and high-throughput connectivity. Option A (AWS VPN) uses the public internet. Option C (Amazon CloudFront) is a CDN. Option D (AWS Global Accelerator) routes traffic over the AWS global network but is not a dedicated private connection from on-premises.',
