  'Option A (correct) is an Application Load Balancer (ALB), which is ideal for distributing HTTP/HTTPS traffic across multiple targets, such as EC2 instances, in different Availability Zones, enhancing fault tolerance and scalability. Option B (Amazon Route 53) is a DNS service. Option C (AWS Global Accelerator) routes traffic at the network layer. Option D (Amazon CloudFront) is a CDN.',
