  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Snowball) is the correct choice. AWS Snowball is part of the AWS Snow Family, which provides physical devices for transferring large amounts of data (petabytes-scale) into and out of AWS. For 200 TB with a slow internet connection, Snowball is much faster and more cost-effective than network transfer. Option B (AWS DataSync) is for online data transfer over a network. Option C (AWS Transfer Family) is for transferring files over SFTP, FTPS, and FTP, not for offline physical data transfer. Option D (Amazon S3 Transfer Acceleration) speeds up transfers over the internet to S3 but still relies on network connectivity.',
