INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_141',
  'A company is deploying a new application that serves both HTTP/HTTPS traffic for its public web interface and uses a custom TCP protocol for a backend gaming server. Which Elastic Load Balancing types can be used to efficiently distribute traffic for these distinct protocols? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Gateway Load Balancer, for deploying and managing third-party virtual appliances.","Application Load Balancer (ALB), for HTTP/HTTPS traffic at the application layer.","Classic Load Balancer, which is a legacy load balancer type.","Network Load Balancer (NLB), for TCP/UDP traffic at the transport layer.","Amazon Route 53, for DNS-based traffic routing."]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (correct) and Option D (correct) are the appropriate Elastic Load Balancing types. The Application Load Balancer (ALB) is designed for HTTP/HTTPS traffic, offering advanced routing features. The Network Load Balancer (NLB) is ideal for TCP/UDP traffic, providing ultra-high performance and static IP addresses. Option A (incorrect) is used for deploying network virtual appliances, not general application traffic. Option C (incorrect) is a legacy load balancer that is not recommended for new applications. Option E (incorrect) is a DNS service, not a load balancer itself, although it can route traffic to load balancers.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  38,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_142',
  'A development team wants to deploy new applications without needing to provision, scale, or manage any underlying servers. They are looking for serverless compute options for their containerized workloads and event-driven functions. Which AWS services provide these serverless capabilities? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon EC2, which provides virtual servers in the cloud.","AWS Lambda, for running code without provisioning servers.","Amazon ECS, for container orchestration that can run on EC2 instances.","AWS Fargate, a serverless compute engine for containers.","Amazon EKS, for running Kubernetes on AWS."]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (correct) and Option D (correct) are serverless compute options. AWS Lambda allows you to run code without provisioning or managing servers, and it now supports deploying functions as container images. AWS Fargate is a serverless compute engine that works with Amazon ECS and Amazon EKS, allowing you to run containers without managing the underlying EC2 instances. Option A (incorrect) requires provisioning and managing servers. Option C (incorrect) and Option E (incorrect) are container orchestration services that can run on EC2 instances, which require server management unless combined with Fargate.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  39,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_143',
  'To decouple microservices and prevent cascading failures in a distributed system, a solutions architect needs to implement asynchronous communication patterns. Which AWS services can effectively facilitate this type of communication between independent microservices? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon API Gateway, for creating, publishing, and managing REST APIs.","Amazon SQS, for message queuing and reliable asynchronous delivery.","AWS Step Functions, for orchestrating workflows of distributed applications.","Amazon EventBridge, for building event-driven architectures.","Elastic Load Balancing, for distributing incoming application traffic."]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (correct) and Option D (correct) are excellent choices for asynchronous communication and decoupling microservices. Amazon SQS provides a fully managed message queuing service that enables asynchronous processing and decouples sending and receiving components. Amazon EventBridge is a serverless event bus that makes it easy to connect applications together using data from your own applications, integrated SaaS applications, and AWS services, facilitating event-driven architectures. Option A (incorrect) is for synchronous API management. Option C (incorrect) is for orchestrating workflows, which can use asynchronous services but is not a primary asynchronous communication service itself. Option E (incorrect) is a load balancer for synchronous traffic.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  40,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_144',
  'A development team needs to create, publish, maintain, monitor, and secure REST APIs for their backend services, which are implemented as AWS Lambda functions. Which AWS services are best suited to fulfill these requirements for API management and backend integration? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon SQS, for message queuing between services.","Amazon API Gateway, for managing and securing API endpoints.","Amazon SNS, for publishing messages to subscribers.","AWS Lambda, for executing the backend logic of the API.","Amazon EventBridge, for building event-driven architectures."]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (correct) and Option D (correct) are best suited for API management and backend integration in this scenario. Amazon API Gateway is a fully managed service that handles all the tasks involved in creating, publishing, maintaining, monitoring, and securing REST APIs. AWS Lambda is commonly used as a backend integration for Amazon API Gateway, executing the actual business logic in a serverless manner when an API endpoint is invoked. Option A (incorrect), Option C (incorrect), and Option E (incorrect) are messaging and eventing services, not directly used for creating or managing REST API endpoints or their direct backend execution.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  41,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_145',
  'To design a scalable and resilient microservices architecture, a solutions architect must ensure that application components are stateless, allowing instances to be added or removed dynamically without affecting user experience. Which of the following practices are crucial for achieving and maintaining statelessness? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Relying on sticky sessions configured on Elastic Load Balancers to maintain user context.","Storing session data and user preferences in external, distributed caching services like Amazon ElastiCache.","Storing user preferences and temporary data directly on Amazon EC2 instance local storage.","Using Amazon DynamoDB for persistent storage of application state and user profiles.","Attaching Amazon EBS volumes to EC2 instances for shared application state."]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (correct) and Option D (correct) are crucial for achieving statelessness. Storing session data and user preferences in external, distributed caching services like Amazon ElastiCache ensures that any application instance can retrieve the necessary state, making the instances themselves stateless. Using Amazon DynamoDB for persistent storage of application state and user profiles also externalizes state, allowing application instances to remain stateless and scale independently. Option A (incorrect) is an anti-pattern for true statelessness, as it binds a user''s session to a specific instance, hindering horizontal scaling and fault tolerance. Option C (incorrect) and Option E (incorrect) tie state to specific instances or local storage, preventing dynamic scaling and making recovery from instance failures difficult.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  42,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_146',
  'A company wants to deploy containerized applications with minimal operational overhead for managing the underlying infrastructure, focusing solely on their application code. They need to choose AWS services that provide a serverless experience for running containers. Which AWS services or launch types fulfill this requirement? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon EC2, which requires manual server provisioning and management.","Amazon ECS, when configured to run tasks on EC2 instances.","AWS Fargate, a serverless compute engine for Amazon ECS and Amazon EKS.","Amazon EKS, when configured to run nodes on EC2 instances.","AWS Lambda, which supports deploying functions as container images."]'::json,
  '{2,4}',
  'Option C (correct) and Option E (correct) provide a serverless experience for running containers. AWS Fargate is a serverless compute engine that allows you to run containers without having to provision, scale, or manage the underlying EC2 instances. AWS Lambda now supports deploying functions as container images, allowing developers to package and deploy their code as containers while still benefiting from Lambda''s serverless operational model. Option A (incorrect), Option B (incorrect), and Option D (incorrect) involve managing EC2 instances, which contradicts the requirement for minimal operational overhead and a serverless experience.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  43,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_147',
  'A development team is building a new microservices application and needs to implement asynchronous, event-driven communication between services to ensure loose coupling. Which AWS services are most suitable for enabling this pattern? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon API Gateway","Amazon SQS","Amazon EventBridge","Amazon CloudFront","Amazon ElastiCache"]'::json,
  '{1,2}',
  'Amazon SQS (Option B) provides a fully managed message queuing service for decoupling and scaling microservices, enabling asynchronous communication. Amazon EventBridge (Option C) is a serverless event bus that makes it easy to connect applications together using data from your own applications, integrated SaaS applications, and AWS services, facilitating event-driven architectures. Option A (Amazon API Gateway) is used for creating, publishing, maintaining, monitoring, and securing REST, HTTP, and WebSocket APIs, primarily for synchronous communication. Option D (Amazon CloudFront) is a content delivery network (CDN) service. Option E (Amazon ElastiCache) is a managed caching service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  44,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_148',
  'A web application experiences high read loads on frequently accessed data, causing performance bottlenecks. To improve response times and reduce the load on the backend database, which AWS services should a Solutions Architect recommend for implementing a caching strategy? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon S3","Amazon ElastiCache","Amazon CloudFront","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon EBS"]'::json,
  '{1,2}',
  'Amazon ElastiCache (Option B) is a managed caching service that supports Redis and Memcached, ideal for in-memory caching of database query results or session data to reduce database load and improve application performance. Amazon CloudFront (Option C) is a content delivery network (CDN) that caches static and dynamic web content at edge locations, reducing latency for end-users and offloading origin servers. Option A (Amazon S3) is object storage, not primarily a caching service for application data. Option D (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database service. Option E (Amazon EBS) provides block storage for EC2 instances.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  45,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_149',
  'A company is deploying a new application on Amazon EC2 instances and requires a service to distribute incoming application traffic across multiple instances to ensure high availability and scalability. Which AWS services can fulfill this requirement? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon Route 53","Elastic Load Balancing (ALB)","AWS Global Accelerator","Elastic Load Balancing (NLB)","Amazon API Gateway"]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Elastic Load Balancing (ALB) (Option B) is an Application Load Balancer that operates at the application layer (Layer 7) and is ideal for HTTP/HTTPS traffic, offering advanced routing features. Elastic Load Balancing (NLB) (Option D) is a Network Load Balancer that operates at the connection layer (Layer 4) and is best suited for extreme performance and static IP addresses for TCP/UDP traffic. Both distribute incoming traffic across targets. Option A (Amazon Route 53) is a DNS web service that routes users to internet resources but does not directly distribute traffic across instances. Option C (AWS Global Accelerator) improves global application availability and performance using the AWS global network. Option E (Amazon API Gateway) is for managing APIs, not for general traffic distribution to EC2 instances.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  46,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_150',
  'A development team wants to deploy containerized applications on AWS with minimal operational overhead for managing the underlying infrastructure. Which AWS services allow them to run containers without provisioning and managing the underlying EC2 instances? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon EC2","AWS Fargate","Amazon ECS","AWS Lambda","Amazon EFS"]'::json,
  '{1,2}',
  'AWS Fargate (Option B) is a serverless compute engine for containers that works with both Amazon ECS and Amazon EKS, allowing you to run containers without provisioning or managing servers. Amazon ECS (Option C) is a highly scalable, fast container management service that supports running containers on EC2 instances or using AWS Fargate as a serverless compute option. When using ECS with the Fargate launch type, you do not manage the underlying EC2 instances. Option A (Amazon EC2) requires manual management of servers. Option D (AWS Lambda) is for serverless functions, not containers in the traditional sense. Option E (Amazon EFS) is a scalable file storage service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  47,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_151',
  'An application running on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Elastic Load Balancer needs to maintain user session state. To ensure the application remains stateless and can scale horizontally without users losing their session data, which AWS services can be used to store session information externally? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon ElastiCache","Amazon EC2 instance store","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon EBS","Amazon S3"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Amazon ElastiCache (Option A) provides a managed in-memory data store (Redis or Memcached) that is ideal for storing session state, allowing application instances to be truly stateless and scale horizontally. Amazon DynamoDB (Option C) is a fast and flexible NoSQL database service that can also be used to store session state, offering high availability and scalability. Option B (Amazon EC2 instance store) is ephemeral storage tied to a specific EC2 instance and would lead to session loss if the instance fails or is terminated. Option D (Amazon EBS) is block storage for a single EC2 instance and is not suitable for shared session state across multiple instances. Option E (Amazon S3) is object storage and not designed for low-latency session state management.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  48,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_152',
  'A company is refactoring a monolithic application into microservices. To achieve loose coupling and improve resilience by preventing cascading failures between services, which AWS services should be used for asynchronous communication? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon API Gateway","Amazon SQS","Amazon SNS","Amazon EventBridge","Elastic Load Balancing (ALB)"]'::json,
  '{1,2,3}',
  'Amazon SQS (Option B) provides a fully managed message queuing service for decoupling and scaling microservices, enabling asynchronous communication. Amazon SNS (Option C) is a fully managed messaging service for A2A and A2P communication, allowing publishers to send messages to a large number of subscribers asynchronously. Amazon EventBridge (Option D) is a serverless event bus that makes it easy to connect applications together using data from various sources, facilitating event-driven, loosely coupled architectures. Option A (Amazon API Gateway) is primarily for synchronous API calls, which can lead to tight coupling if not used carefully. Option E (Elastic Load Balancing ALB) distributes incoming HTTP/HTTPS traffic but does not provide asynchronous messaging capabilities.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_153',
  'A Solutions Architect needs to design an application to handle fluctuating traffic demands by automatically adjusting the number of compute resources. Which AWS services are fundamental for implementing horizontal scaling for Amazon EC2 instances? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling","Vertical scaling on a larger EC2 instance","Elastic Load Balancing (ALB)","Amazon RDS Multi-AZ","Amazon EBS"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling (Option A) automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances in response to demand, providing horizontal scaling. Elastic Load Balancing (ALB) (Option C) distributes incoming traffic across multiple instances, working in conjunction with Auto Scaling to ensure traffic is evenly distributed to new instances. Option B (Vertical scaling on a larger EC2 instance) is a different scaling strategy (vertical) and does not involve adding more instances. Option D (Amazon RDS Multi-AZ) provides high availability for databases but is not a horizontal scaling mechanism for compute. Option E (Amazon EBS) provides block storage and is not directly involved in horizontal compute scaling.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  50,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_154',
  'A company wants to expose backend services as secure, scalable APIs for mobile and web applications. Which AWS services are primarily used for building, deploying, and managing these APIs? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon API Gateway","AWS Lambda","Amazon SQS","Amazon SNS","Amazon CloudFront"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Amazon API Gateway (Option A) is a fully managed service that makes it easy for developers to create, publish, maintain, monitor, and secure APIs at any scale. AWS Lambda (Option B) is a serverless compute service often used as a backend for API Gateway, executing code in response to API requests without managing servers. Option C (Amazon SQS) is a message queuing service. Option D (Amazon SNS) is a notification service. Option E (Amazon CloudFront) is a content delivery network. While these services can be part of an overall solution, API Gateway and Lambda are the core services for API creation and management in a serverless context.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  51,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_155',
  'A team is building a new application that requires both a reliable message queue for asynchronous processing and a way to orchestrate complex workflows involving multiple AWS services. Which AWS managed services should they consider for these specific requirements? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon EventBridge","Amazon SQS","AWS Step Functions","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon SNS"]'::json,
  '{1,2}',
  'Amazon SQS (Option B) is a fully managed message queuing service that enables you to decouple and scale microservices, distributed systems, and serverless applications, making it ideal for reliable asynchronous processing. AWS Step Functions (Option C) is a serverless workflow service that lets you combine AWS Lambda functions and other AWS services to build business-critical applications, perfect for orchestrating complex workflows. Option A (Amazon EventBridge) is an event bus for event-driven architectures but not a traditional message queue or workflow orchestrator. Option D (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database. Option E (Amazon SNS) is a messaging service for publishing messages to subscribers, not primarily a queue or workflow orchestrator.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  52,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_1_156',
  'A Solutions Architect needs to design a system that can process a high volume of incoming events asynchronously and trigger serverless compute based on these events. Which AWS services are best suited for building such an event-driven processing pipeline? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Lambda","Amazon SQS","Amazon SNS","Amazon CloudFront","Amazon ElastiCache"]'::json,
  '{0,1,2}',
  'AWS Lambda (Option A) is a serverless compute service that can be triggered by various event sources, including SQS and SNS, to process events asynchronously. Amazon SQS (Option B) provides a fully managed message queuing service for decoupling and scaling microservices, allowing messages to be processed asynchronously by Lambda functions or other services. Amazon SNS (Option C) is a fully managed messaging service that can publish messages to multiple subscribers, including Lambda functions, enabling asynchronous, fan-out event processing. Option D (Amazon CloudFront) is a content delivery network. Option E (Amazon ElastiCache) is a managed caching service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  53,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_19_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

