  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (Amazon CloudFront) is a content delivery network (CDN) that distributes web content globally from edge locations, reducing latency and improving performance for users. Option D (AWS Global Accelerator) uses the AWS global network to improve the availability and performance of your applications by directing user traffic to the optimal endpoint. Option A (Amazon VPC) provides network isolation within a region. Option C (AWS Direct Connect) provides private connectivity to AWS from on-premises. Option E (Amazon Route 53) is a DNS service that can route traffic, but CloudFront and Global Accelerator specifically optimize global performance over the AWS backbone.',
