  '{1,2}',
  'Option B (Amazon CloudFront) is a Content Delivery Network (CDN) that caches static and dynamic content at edge locations worldwide, significantly reducing latency for users and improving content delivery. Option C (AWS Global Accelerator) uses the AWS global network to route user traffic to the optimal application endpoint, improving performance and availability for both global and local users. Option A (AWS VPN) and Option D (AWS Direct Connect) are for connecting on-premises networks to AWS, not for global application delivery to end-users. Option E (Amazon VPC) is a virtual network within AWS, which is foundational but doesn''t directly address global low-latency access or performance optimization.',
