  '{1,2}',
  'Option B (AWS Direct Connect) provides a dedicated, private network connection from your on-premises data center to AWS, bypassing the public internet entirely. Option C (AWS VPN) establishes a secure, encrypted tunnel over the public internet between your on-premises network and your Amazon VPC, creating a private communication channel. Option A (Amazon CloudFront) and Option D (AWS Global Accelerator) are edge services for content delivery and application acceleration, not for private on-premises to VPC connectivity. Option E (Amazon VPC Peering) connects two VPCs together, not an on-premises network to a VPC.',
