  '{1,3}',
  'Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) (Option B) automatically distributes incoming application traffic across multiple targets, such as EC2 instances, in multiple Availability Zones, improving application availability and fault tolerance. Amazon CloudFront (Option D) is a content delivery network (CDN) service that securely delivers data, videos, applications, and APIs to customers globally with low latency and high transfer speeds, improving performance and availability. Amazon VPC (Option A) is for creating isolated network environments. AWS Direct Connect (Option C) and AWS VPN (Option E) are for connecting on-premises networks to AWS, not for distributing application traffic to end-users.',
