  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Amazon CloudFront) is a content delivery network (CDN) service that securely delivers data, videos, applications, and APIs to customers globally with low latency and high transfer speeds by caching content at edge locations. Option B (AWS Global Accelerator) improves the availability and performance of applications with local and global users by directing traffic to optimal endpoints over the AWS global network. Option C (Amazon Route 53) is a scalable cloud Domain Name System (DNS) web service, which can route traffic but doesn''t cache content at edge locations. Option D (AWS Direct Connect) provides a dedicated network connection from your premises to AWS. Option E (AWS VPN) establishes a secure connection between your on-premises network and your AWS VPC. Neither Direct Connect nor VPN are designed for global content caching or application performance optimization for end-users.',
