VALUES (
  'q_20_m_20_4_106',
  'Which AWS services are primarily used for distributing incoming application traffic across multiple targets, such as Amazon EC2 instances or containers? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Application Load Balancer (ALB)","Network Load Balancer (NLB)","Amazon CloudFront","AWS Global Accelerator","Amazon Route 53"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Application Load Balancer - ALB) operates at the application layer (Layer 7) and is ideal for HTTP/HTTPS traffic, providing advanced routing features. Option B (Network Load Balancer - NLB) operates at the connection layer (Layer 4) and is optimized for extreme performance and static IP addresses, handling TCP, UDP, and TLS traffic. Both ALBs and NLBs are types of Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) and are designed to distribute incoming application traffic. Option C (Amazon CloudFront) is a content delivery network, and Option D (AWS Global Accelerator) improves global application performance, but neither primarily distributes traffic across targets within a VPC. Option E (Amazon Route 53) is a DNS service that routes user requests to internet resources, but it does not distribute traffic across multiple targets in the same way a load balancer does.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain20_4',
  NOW(),
  68,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_20_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_20_m_20_4_107',
  'An organization plans to connect more than 10 VPCs in a hub-and-spoke architecture to centralize network management and routing. Which AWS services are key components for this architecture? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Transit Gateway","Amazon VPC","VPC peering","AWS VPN","Amazon CloudFront"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Transit Gateway) is specifically designed for connecting thousands of VPCs and on-premises networks through a central hub, simplifying network management and enabling a scalable hub-and-spoke architecture. Option B (Amazon VPC) represents the individual virtual networks that act as the ''spokes'' in the hub-and-spoke model, connecting to the Transit Gateway. Option C (VPC peering) is not transitive and becomes unmanageable with a large number of VPCs (e.g., 10+), requiring O(n^2) connections. Option D (AWS VPN) can connect VPCs to on-premises networks but is not the primary service for a scalable hub-and-spoke between many VPCs. Option E (Amazon CloudFront) is a content delivery network and is unrelated to VPC networking architecture.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain20_4',
  NOW(),
  69,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_20_4',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

