  '{2,3}',
  'Option C (Amazon EFS) provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources, allowing multiple EC2 instances to access it concurrently. Option D (Amazon FSx for Lustre) provides a high-performance file system optimized for compute-intensive workloads, also allowing multiple EC2 instances to access it. Option A (Amazon EBS) provides block storage for a single EC2 instance (though Multi-Attach is available for specific use cases, it''s not the primary shared file system solution). Option B (Amazon S3) is object storage and does not provide a file system interface. Option E (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database service.',
  NOW(),
