  'Option C (Amazon EFS) provides a scalable, elastic, shared file system for Linux workloads, supporting the NFS protocol. Option D (Amazon FSx for Windows File Server) provides a fully managed native Microsoft Windows file system, accessible via the SMB protocol, which is a standard file protocol. Option A (Amazon S3) is object storage and does not offer a file system interface. Option B (Amazon EBS) provides block storage, not a file system. Option E (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database service.',
