  'Option B (Amazon S3 Standard-IA) is an S3 storage class for data that is accessed less frequently but requires rapid access when needed, offering lower storage costs than S3 Standard. Option C (Amazon S3 Glacier) is a secure, durable, and extremely low-cost storage service for data archiving, suitable for data that is rarely accessed. Option A (Amazon EBS Provisioned IOPS) is a high-performance block storage type for EC2 instances, not for archiving. Option D (Amazon EFS Infrequent Access) is for file storage with infrequent access, but S3 Glacier is generally more cost-effective for true archiving. Option E (Amazon RDS) is a relational database service, not a general-purpose storage service for backups.',
