  '{2,3}',
  'General Purpose SSD (gp3) (Option C) volumes offer a good balance of price and performance for a wide variety of transactional workloads, with a consistent baseline performance. Provisioned IOPS SSD (io2) (Option D) volumes are designed for I/O-intensive transactional workloads that require sustained IOPS performance and low latency. Throughput Optimized HDD (st1) (Option A) and Cold HDD (sc1) (Option B) are HDD-backed volumes optimized for throughput and cold data respectively, not for low-latency transactional databases. Amazon S3 Standard (Option E) is object storage, not block storage for EC2 instances.',
