  '{1,2}',
  'Option B (Amazon ElastiCache) is a fully managed in-memory caching service that supports Redis and Memcached, ideal for reducing database load and improving application response times. Option C (Amazon CloudFront) is a content delivery network (CDN) that caches content at edge locations, reducing latency for users and offloading origin servers. Option A (Amazon S3) is object storage, not primarily a caching service for application data. Option D (Amazon RDS) is a relational database service, not a caching service. Option E (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database, not a caching service for other databases.',
