  'matching',
  '{"A":"EC2 Auto Scaling","B":"AWS Lambda","C":"Amazon EMR"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'EC2 Auto Scaling (Option A) provides the primary benefit of elastic capacity adjustment, automatically adding or removing EC2 instances to match fluctuating application traffic, ensuring performance and cost efficiency. AWS Lambda (Option B) offers automatic scaling and high availability for event-driven code, executing functions without explicit server provisioning or management. Amazon EMR (Option C) is designed for the scalable processing of vast datasets, providing managed clusters for big data frameworks like Apache Spark and Hadoop, which are essential for high-performance data analytics.',
