  'matching',
  '{"A":"Availability Zone","B":"Region","C":"Edge Location"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'An Availability Zone (Option A) is an isolated location within an AWS Region, designed to be independent failures. A Region (Option B) is a physical geographic area where AWS clusters data centers, consisting of multiple, isolated Availability Zones. An Edge Location (Option C) is a worldwide network of data centers used by Amazon CloudFront and AWS Global Accelerator to deliver content and improve application performance closer to users.',
