  'Match the Amazon S3 storage class to its cost and access frequency.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"S3 Standard","B":"S3 Standard-IA","C":"S3 Glacier Deep Archive"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon S3 Standard (Option A) is for general-purpose storage of frequently accessed data, offering high durability and low latency. Amazon S3 Standard-IA (Infrequent Access) (Option B) is for data that is accessed less frequently but requires rapid retrieval when needed, offering a lower storage price but a retrieval fee. Amazon S3 Glacier Deep Archive (Option C) is the lowest-cost storage class for long-term archiving, with retrieval times typically within hours.',
