  '{"A":"Provisioned IOPS","B":"Capacity Units","C":"Multi-Region Deployment"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Provisioned IOPS (Option A) allows you to specify a consistent baseline of input/output operations per second for EBS volumes or RDS instances, guaranteeing I/O performance. Capacity Units (Option B) are a measure of throughput and storage for Amazon DynamoDB, allowing you to provision read and write capacity based on your application''s needs. Multi-Region Deployment (Option C) involves deploying a database across multiple AWS Regions for disaster recovery, global availability, and low-latency access for geographically dispersed users.',
