  'Provisioned capacity (left 0) for Amazon DynamoDB requires users to specify the number of read and write capacity units needed, which are billed hourly. On-demand capacity (left 1) allows users to pay per request for data reads and writes, making it suitable for unpredictable workloads without needing to specify capacity upfront.',
