  NULL,
  'Read Replicas (left 0) are used to distribute read load across multiple database instances, improving read performance and availability. Caching (left 1) with services like Amazon ElastiCache helps reduce the load on the primary database by serving frequently accessed data from a faster, in-memory store. Database capacity planning (left 2) involves optimizing resource allocation to ensure the database can handle anticipated workloads efficiently and cost-effectively.',
