  NULL,
  'For Amazon RDS (left 0), primary cost drivers include the instance size (vCPU, memory) and the provisioned storage. For Amazon DynamoDB (left 1), costs are driven by read/write capacity units (or requests in on-demand mode) and stored data size. For Amazon ElastiCache (left 2), costs are primarily based on the chosen node type and the amount of memory provisioned.',
