  NULL,
  'A Relational Database (left: 0) is suitable for structured data with complex queries and ACID properties (right: 2), making it ideal for traditional business applications. A NoSQL Database (left: 1) is ideal for flexible schema and high scalability for unstructured data (right: 0), commonly used for mobile, web, and gaming applications. An In-memory Database (left: 2), such as provided by Amazon ElastiCache, is best for analytical processing and caching with low latency (right: 1), significantly speeding up data retrieval for real-time applications.',
