  'matching',
  '{"A":"Multi-AZ Deployment","B":"Single-AZ Deployment","C":"Read Replica"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Multi-AZ Deployment (left: 0) provides high availability and automatic failover, but doubles database instance costs (right: 2) due to the synchronous standby. Single-AZ Deployment (left: 1) offers lower cost, suitable for development or non-critical production databases (right: 0) where high availability is not paramount. A Read Replica (left: 2) enhances read performance and offloads the primary database, and can be cross-Region (right: 1), which helps in scaling read-heavy applications and distributing data geographically.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain21_4',
  NOW(),
  29,
  '{"left":["Multi-AZ Deployment","Single-AZ Deployment","Read Replica"],"right":["Lower cost, suitable for development or non-critical production databases","Enhances read performance and offloads primary database, can be cross-Region","High availability and automatic failover, but doubles database instance costs"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_21_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_21_m_21_3_105',
  'A company needs to optimize the cost of its database solutions for various workloads. Match each database service or feature to its primary cost-optimization use case.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon Aurora Serverless v2","B":"DynamoDB On-Demand capacity mode","C":"Amazon RDS Read Replicas"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 (Option A) is designed for intermittent or unpredictable relational database workloads, scaling capacity in fine-grained increments and down to minimal ACUs during idle periods to avoid paying for unused provisioned capacity. DynamoDB On-Demand capacity mode (Option B) is cost-effective for unpredictable NoSQL traffic patterns because you pay per request, eliminating the need for capacity planning and preventing over-provisioning. Amazon RDS Read Replicas (Option C) are used to offload read traffic from the primary database instance, reducing the load and potentially allowing for a smaller, less expensive primary instance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain21_4',
  NOW(),
  30,
  '{"left":["Amazon Aurora Serverless v2","DynamoDB On-Demand capacity mode","Amazon RDS Read Replicas"],"right":["Intermittent or unpredictable relational workloads","Unpredictable NoSQL traffic patterns","Offloading read traffic from primary database"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_21_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_21_m_21_3_106',
  'A solutions architect is designing a database solution for a new application with varying traffic patterns. Match the database capacity strategy to the workload characteristic it cost-effectively supports.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"DynamoDB Provisioned Capacity","B":"DynamoDB On-Demand Capacity","C":"Aurora Serverless v2"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'DynamoDB Provisioned Capacity (Option A) is cost-effective for predictable, consistent NoSQL traffic where you can accurately forecast read and write requirements. DynamoDB On-Demand Capacity (Option B) is ideal for unpredictable, spiky NoSQL traffic because you pay per request, avoiding over-provisioning or throttling. Aurora Serverless v2 (Option C) is designed for intermittent relational database usage, automatically scaling capacity up and down based on demand, including scaling to zero for idle periods, which significantly optimizes costs.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain21_4',
  NOW(),
  31,
  '{"left":["DynamoDB Provisioned Capacity","DynamoDB On-Demand Capacity","Aurora Serverless v2"],"right":["Predictable, consistent NoSQL traffic","Unpredictable, spiky NoSQL traffic","Intermittent relational database usage"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_21_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_21_m_21_3_107',
  'A company needs to reduce costs for its existing Amazon RDS databases. Match the cost-optimization technique to its primary benefit.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Disabling Multi-AZ for non-production DBs","B":"Using Amazon ElastiCache","C":"Implementing data retention policies"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Disabling Multi-AZ for non-production databases (Option A) significantly reduces costs by eliminating the synchronous standby replica, which effectively halves the instance cost for development and testing environments. Using Amazon ElastiCache (Option B) reduces the load on the primary database by serving frequently accessed data from an in-memory cache, which can lead to lower database instance size requirements and associated costs. Implementing data retention policies (Option C) helps optimize storage costs by automatically deleting old, unneeded data from the database, preventing indefinite storage of irrelevant information.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain21_4',
  NOW(),
  32,
  '{"left":["Disabling Multi-AZ for non-production DBs","Using Amazon ElastiCache","Implementing data retention policies"],"right":["Halving standby instance costs for dev/test","Reducing database load and associated costs","Automating deletion of old, unneeded data"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_21_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_21_m_21_3_108',
  'A development team is using Amazon RDS for a new application. They want to ensure cost-efficiency for both development and production environments. Match the RDS configuration to its cost-optimized use case.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"RDS Single-AZ deployment","B":"RDS Read Replicas","C":"Amazon RDS Proxy"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'An RDS Single-AZ deployment (Option A) is cost-effective for non-critical development and test environments as it avoids the doubled cost of a Multi-AZ setup, which is primarily for high availability. RDS Read Replicas (Option B) are used to scale read capacity and offload read traffic from the primary database, potentially allowing the primary instance to be smaller and reducing overall database costs. Amazon RDS Proxy (Option C) manages database connections efficiently, reducing the overhead on the database instance and allowing applications to scale without exhausting database connections, which can prevent the need for larger, more expensive database instances.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain21_4',
  NOW(),
  33,
  '{"left":["RDS Single-AZ deployment","RDS Read Replicas","Amazon RDS Proxy"],"right":["Cost-effective for non-critical dev/test environments","Scales read capacity, reduces primary DB load","Manages database connections efficiently, reducing overhead"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_21_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_21_m_21_3_109',
  'A company is designing a new application that requires a highly scalable and cost-effective database solution. Match the database service to its primary cost-optimization benefit.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon DynamoDB","B":"Amazon Aurora","C":"Amazon ElastiCache"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon DynamoDB (Option A) is a serverless NoSQL database that scales on demand and offers a pay-per-request model, making it highly cost-effective for variable workloads. Amazon Aurora (Option B) provides high performance and MySQL/PostgreSQL compatibility with a decoupled storage and compute architecture, allowing storage to scale independently and reducing costs by only paying for what is used. Amazon ElastiCache (Option C) provides in-memory caching, which reduces the load on the primary database, leading to lower database instance costs and improved performance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain21_4',
  NOW(),
  34,
  '{"left":["Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon Aurora","Amazon ElastiCache"],"right":["Serverless NoSQL, scales on demand, pay per request","High performance, MySQL/PostgreSQL compatibility, decoupled storage","In-memory caching, reduces database load and cost"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_21_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_21_m_21_3_110',
  'A solutions architect is optimizing database costs for a new application with unpredictable usage patterns. Match the database feature to its cost-optimization advantage for this scenario.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Aurora Serverless v2 scaling","B":"DynamoDB On-Demand capacity","C":"RDS Single-AZ deployment"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Aurora Serverless v2 scaling (Option A) allows compute capacity to scale in fine-grained increments and down to a minimal state (or even zero for v1) during idle periods, making it highly cost-effective for unpredictable or intermittent relational workloads. DynamoDB On-Demand capacity (Option B) automatically adjusts read/write capacity based on actual usage, where you pay per request, eliminating the need for capacity planning and preventing over-provisioning for unpredictable NoSQL traffic. An RDS Single-AZ deployment (Option C) avoids the cost of a standby replica, making it a cost-optimized choice for non-critical development or testing workloads where high availability is not paramount.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain21_4',
  NOW(),
  35,
  '{"left":["Aurora Serverless v2 scaling","DynamoDB On-Demand capacity","RDS Single-AZ deployment"],"right":["Scales compute capacity in fine increments, down to zero","Automatically adjusts read/write capacity, pay per request","Avoids cost of standby replica for non-critical workloads"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_21_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

