  '{"A":"Route tables","B":"Security Groups","C":"Network ACLs"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Route tables (left 0) define the network paths for traffic leaving a subnet. Security Groups (left 1) act as an instance-level firewall, controlling inbound and outbound traffic for EC2 instances. Network ACLs (left 2) function as a subnet-level firewall, controlling traffic in and out of subnets with stateless rules.',
