  '{"A":"Traffic between EC2 instances in different Availability Zones","B":"Traffic between VPCs in different AWS Regions","C":"Traffic from EC2 instances in private subnets to the public internet"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Traffic between EC2 instances in different Availability Zones (left: 0) incurs inter-AZ data transfer costs, typically lower than inter-Region (right: 2). Traffic between VPCs in different AWS Regions (left: 1) should be routed over the AWS global backbone via VPC peering or Transit Gateway for lower latency and cost (right: 1), avoiding the public internet. Traffic from EC2 instances in private subnets to the public internet (left: 2) must route through a NAT Gateway, incurring hourly and per GB charges (right: 0), making it a significant cost component.',
  NOW(),
