  'matching',
  '{"A":"NAT Gateway","B":"VPC Endpoint","C":"VPC Peering"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'A NAT Gateway (left: 0) allows private subnets to access the public internet or AWS services (right: 1) outside the VPC, while preventing inbound connections. A VPC Endpoint (left: 1) enables private access to AWS services from within a VPC (right: 2) without traversing the internet, enhancing security and reducing data transfer costs for certain services. VPC Peering (left: 2) connects two VPCs privately (right: 0), allowing them to communicate as if they were in the same network.',
