  'A Security Group (left[0]) functions as an ''Instance-level firewall'' (right[2]), controlling traffic to and from EC2 instances at the elastic network interface level. A Network ACL (left[1]) operates as a ''Subnet-level firewall'' (right[0]), providing a stateless packet filtering layer for all traffic entering or leaving a subnet. An Amazon VPC (left[2]) creates an ''Isolated virtual network'' (right[1]) in the AWS cloud, logically separated from other virtual networks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain_18_4',
