  NULL,
  'AWS Secrets Manager (Option A) is ideal for automatic rotation of database credentials, API keys, and other secrets, enhancing security by limiting the lifespan of credentials. AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store (Option B) provides secure, hierarchical storage for configuration data management and secrets, suitable for storing application configuration values. IAM Roles (Option C) are the best practice for providing temporary, short-lived credentials to Amazon EC2 instances, eliminating the need to hardcode or embed long-term access keys.',
