  NULL,
  'For SSH access to Amazon EC2 instances (Option A), AWS Systems Manager Session Manager is the best practice as it provides secure and auditable shell access without opening inbound ports or managing SSH keys. For public-facing web applications (Option B), AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) provides free, auto-renewing SSL/TLS certificates to secure communication. For database credentials (Option C), AWS Secrets Manager is the recommended service for storing, managing, and automatically rotating them, enhancing security.',
