  NULL,
  'AWS Systems Manager Session Manager (left[0]) provides secure and auditable instance management without needing to open inbound ports, offering ''Browser-based shell access'' (right[2]). A Bastion Host (left[1]) is a server specifically designed to withstand attacks and acts as a ''Jump server for SSH'' (right[0]) to other instances in a private subnet. Opening port 22 (SSH) to 0.0.0.0/0 in security groups (left[2]) is an anti-pattern (ap-1.2-001) as it exposes instances to brute-force attacks from the entire internet, representing ''Insecure SSH access'' (right[1]).',
