  'matching',
  '{"A":"VPC Endpoint","B":"Private Subnet","C":"Public Subnet"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'A VPC Endpoint (left[0]) enables you to privately connect your VPC to supported AWS services and VPC endpoint services powered by AWS PrivateLink without requiring an internet gateway, NAT device, VPN connection, or AWS Direct Connect connection, matching ''Private connectivity to services'' (right[1]). A Private Subnet (left[1]) is a subnet whose traffic is routed to a NAT gateway or NAT instance for outbound internet access but has ''No direct internet access'' (right[2]) for inbound connections. A Public Subnet (left[2]) has a route to an internet gateway, allowing resources within it to have ''Direct internet access'' (right[0]).',
