  'matching',
  '{"A":"AWS PrivateLink","B":"Amazon Cognito","C":"Security Groups"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS PrivateLink (left[0]) provides private connectivity between VPCs, AWS services, and on-premises applications, enabling ''Private access to services'' (right[2]) without exposing traffic to the public internet. Amazon Cognito (left[1]) offers services for ''User authentication and authorization'' (right[1]) for web and mobile applications, including user directories and identity federation. Security Groups (left[2]) act as virtual firewalls that ''Controls instance traffic'' (right[0]) by specifying which inbound and outbound network traffic is allowed to and from your EC2 instances.',
