INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_2_172',
  'A global enterprise with critical applications needs to implement a comprehensive disaster recovery (DR) strategy to minimize downtime and data loss in the event of a regional outage. They have applications with varying recovery time objectives (RTO) and recovery point objectives (RPO), ranging from hours to near-zero. The team is evaluating different DR patterns to align with these diverse business requirements and budget constraints. Match each disaster recovery strategy to its typical RTO/RPO characteristics.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Backup and Restore","B":"Pilot Light","C":"Warm Standby","D":"Multi-site Active/Active"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Backup and Restore (Option A) typically has the highest RTO and RPO but is the lowest cost DR strategy. Pilot Light (Option B) keeps core services running in the DR Region, offering a lower RTO (tens of minutes) than backup and restore, but still requires full deployment. Warm Standby (Option C) maintains a scaled-down, but fully functional, replica of the production environment, providing a faster RTO (minutes) than pilot light. Multi-site Active/Active (Option D) runs full capacity in multiple Regions simultaneously, offering the lowest RTO and RPO (near-zero) but at the highest cost.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  14,
  '{"left":["Backup and Restore","Pilot Light","Warm Standby","Multi-site Active/Active"],"right":["Highest RTO/RPO, lowest cost","Core services running, minimal RTO","Scaled-down replica, faster RTO","Full capacity in multiple Regions, near-zero RTO/RPO"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_19_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_2_173',
  'A healthcare provider is designing its new patient management system on AWS, prioritizing high availability and fault tolerance to ensure continuous service delivery. They need to protect against failures within a single data center and also plan for potential widespread regional outages, ensuring data integrity and application accessibility. The architecture must support both local resilience and global disaster recovery. Match each AWS architectural approach to its primary scope of resilience.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Multi-AZ deployment","B":"Multi-Region architecture","C":"Amazon RDS Multi-AZ"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'A Multi-AZ deployment (Option A) provides resilience within a single AWS Region by distributing resources across multiple Availability Zones, protecting against single data center failures. A Multi-Region architecture (Option B) extends resilience across different AWS Regions, offering global disaster recovery capabilities against widespread regional outages. Amazon RDS Multi-AZ (Option C) specifically ensures automatic failover for relational databases to a synchronous standby replica in a different Availability Zone, providing high availability for the database layer.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  15,
  '{"left":["Multi-AZ deployment","Multi-Region architecture","Amazon RDS Multi-AZ"],"right":["Provides resilience within a single AWS Region","Offers global disaster recovery capabilities","Ensures automatic failover for relational databases"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_19_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_2_174',
  'An online media company operates a critical web application that must remain available even if one of its backend endpoints becomes unhealthy. They are using Amazon Route 53 for DNS management and need to configure it to automatically redirect traffic away from failed resources. Additionally, they are looking for a service to improve global performance and availability for their users by routing traffic to the optimal endpoint. Match each AWS service or feature to its role in enhancing application availability and performance.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon Route 53 Failover Routing","B":"Route 53 Health Checks","C":"AWS Global Accelerator"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon Route 53 Failover Routing (Option A) is a DNS routing policy that redirects traffic to a healthy endpoint when the primary endpoint becomes unavailable. Route 53 Health Checks (Option B) are essential for failover routing, as they actively monitor the health and availability of endpoints and trigger the DNS failover when a failure is detected (anti-pattern ap-2.2-004). AWS Global Accelerator (Option C) improves the availability and performance of applications by routing user traffic through the AWS global network infrastructure to the optimal endpoint.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  16,
  '{"left":["Amazon Route 53 Failover Routing","Route 53 Health Checks","AWS Global Accelerator"],"right":["DNS policy to redirect traffic on failure","Monitors endpoint availability to trigger failover","Improves global performance and availability via AWS network"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_19_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_2_175',
  'A data analytics company needs to select appropriate storage solutions for various workloads, ranging from frequently accessed operational data for EC2 instances to large archives of unstructured data and shared file systems for compute clusters. Each workload has specific requirements for performance, durability, and access patterns. The goal is to choose the most cost-effective and performant storage type for each use case. Match each AWS storage service to its primary characteristic or typical use case.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon S3 Standard","B":"Amazon EBS gp3","C":"Amazon EFS"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon S3 Standard (Option A) is a highly durable, scalable, and cost-effective object storage service for general-purpose data, suitable for a wide range of use cases including data lakes and backups. Amazon EBS gp3 (Option B) is a general-purpose SSD volume type for Amazon EC2 instances, offering a balance of price and performance for a wide variety of transactional workloads. Amazon EFS (Option C) provides a scalable, elastic, shared file system for Amazon EC2, ideal for use cases requiring shared access to data across multiple instances or containers.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  17,
  '{"left":["Amazon S3 Standard","Amazon EBS gp3","Amazon EFS"],"right":["Highly durable object storage for general purpose","Balanced performance SSD for EC2 instances","Scalable, shared file system for multiple EC2s"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_19_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_2_176',
  'A software company is optimizing its database architecture for a high-traffic application. They are using Amazon RDS for their relational database and need to ensure both high availability and the ability to scale read operations independently. The team is evaluating different RDS features to achieve these goals while avoiding common misconceptions about their functionalities. Match each Amazon RDS feature or service to its primary purpose.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon RDS Multi-AZ deployment","B":"Amazon RDS Read Replica","C":"Amazon Aurora"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon RDS Multi-AZ deployment (Option A) provides automatic failover to a synchronous standby replica in a different Availability Zone for high availability, but the standby does not serve read traffic (anti-pattern ap-2.2-001). Amazon RDS Read Replica (Option B) is specifically designed to scale read operations for increased throughput by creating asynchronous copies of the primary database. Amazon Aurora (Option C) is a highly available, scalable, and fully managed relational database compatible with MySQL and PostgreSQL, offering superior performance and availability compared to standard RDS.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  18,
  '{"left":["Amazon RDS Multi-AZ deployment","Amazon RDS Read Replica","Amazon Aurora"],"right":["Provides automatic failover for high availability","Scales read operations for increased throughput","Highly available, scalable, MySQL/PostgreSQL-compatible database"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_19_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_2_177',
  'A cybersecurity firm is setting up a new virtual private cloud (VPC) on AWS to host its secure analysis tools and sensitive data. They need to segment their network to isolate public-facing web servers from backend databases and internal processing instances. Proper routing must be configured to allow internet access only where necessary and to control traffic flow within the VPC. Match each VPC component to its primary function in network segmentation and traffic management.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Public Subnet","B":"Private Subnet","C":"Route Table"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'A Public Subnet (Option A) is configured with a route to an Internet Gateway, allowing resources within it to be directly accessible from the internet. A Private Subnet (Option B) does not have a route to an Internet Gateway and typically routes outbound traffic through a NAT Gateway, meaning its resources do not have direct internet access. A Route Table (Option C) contains a set of rules, called routes, that determine where network traffic from your subnet or gateway is directed.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  19,
  '{"left":["Public Subnet","Private Subnet","Route Table"],"right":["Hosts resources directly accessible from the internet","Hosts resources without direct internet access","Defines rules for network traffic forwarding"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_19_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_19_m_19_2_178',
  'An online learning platform needs to ensure its application remains highly available and responsive, even when individual instances fail or demand fluctuates. They are implementing a self-healing architecture that can automatically replace unhealthy instances and adjust capacity based on real-time load. Additionally, a robust data protection strategy is required for critical application data. Match each AWS service or feature to its primary contribution to a self-healing and resilient architecture.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling","B":"Elastic Load Balancing Health Checks","C":"AWS Backup"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling (Option A) automatically adjusts EC2 capacity to maintain application availability and allows you to automatically replace unhealthy instances, contributing to self-healing. Elastic Load Balancing Health Checks (Option B) continuously monitor the health of registered targets (e.g., EC2 instances) and stop sending traffic to unhealthy ones, ensuring only healthy instances receive requests. AWS Backup (Option C) provides a centralized, managed service to back up your AWS resources, ensuring data protection and enabling recovery in case of data loss or corruption.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain19_4',
  NOW(),
  20,
  '{"left":["Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling","Elastic Load Balancing Health Checks","AWS Backup"],"right":["Automatically adjusts EC2 capacity and replaces unhealthy instances","Monitors the health of registered targets","Centralized backup management for AWS resources"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_19_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

