  NULL,
  'Horizontal scaling with Auto Scaling (left item 0) distributes load across multiple smaller, more cost-effective instances, scaling dynamically to meet demand without over-provisioning. Hibernation for EC2 instances (left item 1) reduces costs by stopping instances while preserving their RAM contents and private IP addresses, allowing for faster restarts and avoiding full re-initialization. Right-sizing EC2 instances (left item 2) avoids over-provisioning by selecting instance types that precisely match the actual CPU, memory, and network requirements of the workload, preventing unnecessary expenditure on unused capacity.',
