  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon RDS","B":"Amazon DynamoDB","C":"Amazon Aurora"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon RDS (left: 0) is a managed relational database service that supports several database engines like MySQL, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server. Amazon DynamoDB (left: 1) is a fast and flexible NoSQL database service for all applications that need consistent, single-digit millisecond latency at any scale, supporting key-value and document data models. Amazon Aurora (left: 2) is a MySQL and PostgreSQL-compatible relational database built for the cloud, combining the performance and availability of traditional enterprise databases with the simplicity and cost-effectiveness of open-source databases.',
